#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:5
msgid "Search"
msgstr "Поиск"

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:7
msgid ""
"Every executed search will be conserved during your session. You can change "
"a parameter or else, and come back to the list, you will find all your "
"previous search parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:10
msgid "Filtering members list"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:12
msgid ""
"The form at the top of the members list allow you to make some search among "
"members. The :ref:`advanced search <advsearch>` provides more criteria and "
"possibilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:14
msgid "Filter members list"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:19
msgid "You can filter on:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:21
msgid "a full text search on one of the following information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:23
msgid "name (first name, last name and nickname),"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:24
msgid "company name,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:25
msgid "address (address, address continuation, zipcode, town and country),"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:26
msgid ""
"email and instant messaging addresses (email address, website URL, and all "
"direct messaging addresses),"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:27
msgid "job position,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:28
msgid ""
"information (public information and - for administrators only - private "
"information)."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:30
msgid "a member status:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:32
msgid "all members,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:33
msgid "up to date members,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:34
msgid "closes expiries (members whose membership expires in 30 days)"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:35
msgid "latecomers,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:36
msgid "members whose never had a membership,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:37
msgid "staff members,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:38
msgid "administrators."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:40
msgid "a status of the account:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:42
msgid "all accounts,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:43
msgid "active accounts,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:44
msgid "inactive accounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:46
msgid "group affiliation,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:47
msgid "presence or absence of an email address."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:49
msgid ""
"All filters can be combined, giving you the ability to search among your "
"active members whose have an email address and whose name contains a \"a\" ;)"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:54 ../usermanual/recherche.rst:64
msgid "Advanced search"
msgstr "Расширенный поиск"

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:56
msgid ""
"Advanced search can be found in the main menu and propose an certain amount "
"of fields types, related to members or their membership. The screen is "
"separated into five parts (you can reduce individually):"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:58
msgid "**simple search** which recall all filters present in the members list,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:59
msgid ""
"**advanced search** which proposes extra fields on members that can be of "
"use,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:60
msgid ""
"**advanced groups search** (experimental) which allow to search members "
"belonging to all, or to any, of several selected groups,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:61
msgid "**within contributions** allowing search on members contributions,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:62
msgid ""
"**free search** (experimental) which allow to select any member field "
"possible, including dynamic fields, and which will automatically adapt to "
"selected field. You can add and remove lines to refine search."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:72
msgid "Relative dates"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:76
msgid ""
"Every date of the advanced search can be a date relative to the day the "
"search is run, instead of a fixed date. This applies to the dates of the "
"**advanced search** and **within contributions** parts, to the date fields "
"of the **free search**, including dynamic fields, and to the date dynamic "
"fields of contributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:78
msgid ""
"Click on the button next to a date field to switch to a relative date, and "
"click on it again to come back to a fixed date. A relative date is a "
"reference date, optionally shifted by a number of days, weeks, months or "
"years, forward (``+``) or backward (``-``). Reference dates are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:80
msgid "**today**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:81
msgid "**start of the month** and **end of the month**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:82
msgid "**start of the year** and **end of the year**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:83
msgid ""
"**start of the membership period** and **end of the membership period**."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:85
msgid "Relative dates in advanced search"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:90
msgid ""
"The membership period is only known when memberships share the same "
"beginning date (**Beginning of membership** in :ref:`preferences "
"<pref_parameters>`). When memberships are extended for a number of months "
"from the contribution instead, there is no common period, and those two "
"reference dates are not offered."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:92
msgid "Some examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:94
msgid ""
"**Insurance certificates expiring within a month**: on a date dynamic field, "
"a due date between *today* and *today + 1 month*,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:95
msgid "**Adult members**: birth date before *today - 18 years*,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:96
msgid ""
"**Contributions of the current period**: contribution begin date after "
"*start of the membership period*."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:98
msgid ""
"A relative date is computed again each time the search is run: a :ref:`saved "
"search <saved_searches>` using *today + 30 days* always lists what is due "
"within 30 days, whatever the day it is executed. Months and years are added "
"calendar-wise: one month after January 31st is the last day of February."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:103
msgid "Saved searches"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:107
msgid ""
"Every search on members can be stored (with a name) in order to be executed "
"again later. They are accessible only for their author."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:109
msgid ""
"After you proceed a search (\"simple\" or \"advanced\"), just click on the "
"\"Save\" button, and pick up a name."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:111
msgid "Save a search"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:116
msgid "You can find saved searches in the list:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:118
msgid "Searches list"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:123
msgid ""
"From this list, you will be able to remove or execute again searches, and "
"also see a detail of used criteria. :ref:`Relative dates <relative_dates>` "
"are shown in plain words, followed by the date they currently stand for."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:127
msgid ""
"A saved search can be edited from the list: you can rename it, and replace "
"its criteria with the advanced search you are currently using on the members "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:129
msgid ""
"When a saved search is executed, criteria referring to something that no "
"longer exists, such as a removed group, status, contribution type, payment "
"type or dynamic field, are ignored, and a message lists them. Check the "
"search before using it, for example to send a mailing: without those "
"criteria, it may select more members than expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/recherche.rst:131
msgid ""
"Dates of saved searches are stored independently of the language, a search "
"saved in one language can be executed in another one."
msgstr ""
